      "name": "Shield Spell Reinforcement",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "V6RsK1B39FTgmYMv",
        "folder": "h3LLD3BmWA4ndNhV",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Shield Spell Reinforcement",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "free"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You are wielding a shield.</p><hr /><p>You can empower your defensive magic by channeling it through a physical shield. If your next action is to cast the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Shield] cantrip, you use your shield as a locus to cast the spell, raising a magical barrier in the form of a large force projection of your worn shield. You can choose for an adjacent ally to gain the benefits of the <em>shield</em> spell instead of yourself. If the ally would take damage from a physical attack while protected by your <em>shield</em> cantrip, you can use your reaction to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Shield Block] with the spell on their behalf.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 4
          },
